WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:07.090
Elden Ring has an optional tutorial now..so
hey, so go and turn off those annoying pop-ups

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:11.230
in the settings..watch this video, and be
free!

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:16.139
Free to go off..and die in a ditch somewhere.

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:17.500
1 - Charge Attacks

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.500
First, charge attacks.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:24.179
In Elden Ring, they're incredibly powerful..and
who better to test them out on, than White-faced

00:00:24.179 --> 00:00:25.179
Varre?

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:31.150
You maidenless runt..who do you think I am?

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.620
Charge attacks being powerful is one thing,
but what's really special, and important for

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.230
you to know..is just how MANY new TYPES of
attack can be charged.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:44.860
Of course, weapon R2's can be charged for
more damage and posture damage..and even some

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.300
L2 weapon skills can be, like the Glintsword,
or the blood blade.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.380
By holding R1, you can also now charge your
spells.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:57.920
What's special about this, is that charged
variants of spells often have more than just

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.420
a damage multiplier.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.810
Some, like dragonfire..can be channeled longer.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:09.140
Others, like bubbles, persist longer before
popping..and when I used rejection, I noticed

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.800
its regular R1 didn't instantly dismount enemies..but
its charged attack did.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.600
Experiment with charged magic..learn it fully:
because these charged spells cost the same

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.890
amount of FP as their regular variants.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:28.550
Therefore, if you have the time or poise to
charge a spell, you probably should.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:29.550
2 - Crafting

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:34.030
Another thing to get in the habit of is crafting,
which you can do as soon as you buy the crafting

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.870
kit from Kale.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:39.680
After a few hours of play, you should have
accumulated a few recipe books to expand your

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.650
crafting options, and if you've been hunting
and foraging between bosses, then you'll be

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:47.470
able to make quite a bit here.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:52.020
Pay attention to which material drops you
find in the world: It'll make it that tiny

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:58.110
bit easier to gather more of it when you realise
you need it to craft something specific.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:02.491
The crafting page gives you hints at where
to find specific materials, and from what

00:02:02.491 --> 00:02:08.779
I can tell, world materials respawn instantly
upon resting at a grace, making them fairly

00:02:08.779 --> 00:02:10.259
easy to farm.

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:15.779
If there's one thing you want to farm in the
full game, it's sleep arrows.

00:02:15.779 --> 00:02:19.430
These things are insanely powerful, offering
crazy crowd control mid combat, enhancing

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:24.349
your stealth, and opening enemies up for critical
attacks.

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:31.829
One interesting item here are cracked pots,
a container material you need to make thrown

00:02:31.829 --> 00:02:34.739
consumables, like firebombs or sleep pots.

00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:39.159
These cracked pots are magical, going back
into your inventory after you've thrown the

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.709
item you made with them.

00:02:40.709 --> 00:02:43.790
That means if I buy 3 pots, then I can craft
3 firebombs.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:49.489
Then, I can only craft 3 more firebombs if
I throw the 3 I've made.

00:02:49.489 --> 00:02:55.159
Remember: they're a container, not a consumable..and
I reckon it's likely merchants later in the

00:02:55.159 --> 00:03:04.299
game will sell you even more cracked pots,
and allow you to hold even more crafted bombs

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:05.299
at any one time.

00:03:05.299 --> 00:03:06.299
3 - Spirit Summons

00:03:06.299 --> 00:03:10.379
I didn't use any crafting items on my first
playthrough..and that was a mistake.

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:15.249
I spent over an hour on the first major boss
because I was stubborn, determined to beat

00:03:15.249 --> 00:03:22.219
him with an underleveled, underpowered character,
with a weapon I didn't really like.

00:03:22.219 --> 00:03:23.219
Don't make that same mistake.

00:03:23.219 --> 00:03:27.720
Remember, this isn't Sekiro - if something
is giving you trouble, you don't JUST have

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:28.750
to git gud.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:33.969
Instead, take a step back, and remember there
ARE creative ways around your problem.

00:03:33.969 --> 00:03:40.439
First and foremost are spirit summons, powerful
companions that can be found around the world.

00:03:40.439 --> 00:03:44.099
I get the impression that these will work
differently in the final game, but for now,

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:50.279
they are items that use FP, able to be equipped
to your quick-select bar in the equipment

00:03:50.279 --> 00:03:51.279
menu.

00:03:51.279 --> 00:03:55.799
They're able to be summoned in any area that
has this little obelisk..but that's not what

00:03:55.799 --> 00:03:57.209
you should be looking for.

00:03:57.209 --> 00:04:01.560
Instead, if you're in a difficult area, you'll
know it, because THIS icon will pop up on

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.859
the left, letting you know that you can summon
your spirits.

00:04:04.859 --> 00:04:09.189
Some spirits, like the noble sorcerer, are
a sort of ranged DPS.

00:04:09.189 --> 00:04:20.519
Others, like the wolves are melee fighters
with a lot of mobility.

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:25.490
If you're a faith build, you should also consider
healing them between battles with a heal spell

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:29.340
- hell, you can successfully heal them DURING
battle considering how quickly this spell

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.650
comes out.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:36.139
So if you're really having trouble, decide
on the best spirit to suit the situation,

00:04:36.139 --> 00:04:37.320
and try to overcome it that way.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:38.320
4 - Stake of Marika

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:42.220
And if you fail..well, if a fight is difficult
enough to allow for spirit summons, then it

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:46.380
likely has a Stake of Marika as well.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:50.520
If you're within its range, then you'll be
able to choose it as a respawn point upon

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:56.440
death.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:00.370
Basically they're just here to prevent a long
run back from a site of grace.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:03.960
They're easy to miss, but again,you shouldn't
always be looking out for the physical statue.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:08.870
If you're within range of one, you'll get
a small status icon here, in the top left.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.909
5 - Guard Counter

00:05:11.909 --> 00:05:18.090
Try to make use of all of Elden Ring's mechanics
to stay alive.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.759
One of the biggest additions to combat are
"Guard Counters".

00:05:20.759 --> 00:05:25.870
Now, after you block an attack, whether with
a shield or a two-handed weapon, you can follow

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:30.990
up with a strong R2, accompanied by this sound
effect.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:36.729
These attacks come out fast, they deal good
damage, and most importantly: enormous posture

00:05:36.729 --> 00:05:43.139
damage.

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:47.800
Break an enemy's invisible posture meter,
and you'll be able to knock them down for

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.250
a critical strike.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:53.870
So if you have a powerful shield, and are
confident that an enemy has just used the

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:59.770
last attack in their combo, then you have
so much to gain from using a guard counter.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:04.280
Hell, even if you're two-handing a weapon,
Guard Counters give you a reason to block.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.280
They're that good.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.280
6 - Two-handing

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:12.879
So Elden Ring uses X or A as the jump button,
which means interact has moved to Triangle

00:06:12.879 --> 00:06:17.680
and Y..which means the 2-handing input has
changed as well.

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:26.699
Now, to 2-hand a weapon or shield, you have
to HOLD triangle, then tap R1 or L1, depending

00:06:26.699 --> 00:06:29.319
on which one you want to 2-hand.

00:06:29.319 --> 00:06:32.680
It's a bit jarring at first, but actually,
this is a really nice input.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:37.080
It's fast, and lets you quickly two-hand either
weapon, not just one of them.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:43.090
Like in Dark Souls, 2-handing weapons increases
your damage output, and lets you get around

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:46.150
a lack of a strength stat, in many cases.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:52.979
Additionally, Two-handing is even stronger
in Elden Ring because of the new posture system.

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:57.321
A 2-handed weapon will inflict greater posture
damage to your enemies, especially if you

00:06:57.321 --> 00:07:03.620
use R2, charged R2's, or R2 jumping attacks.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:08.210
7 - Ash of War

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:20.300
And that's not all, because 2-handing a weapon
gives you access to its assigned skill.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:24.719
A weapon skill is something you activate with
L2, and the current one you will perform is

00:07:24.719 --> 00:07:28.780
always written here, on the left side of the
screen.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:45.400
Every weapon and shield comes with a default
skill, and while some of them are very unique

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:50.879
and locked to their weapon, like this one.........most
of them aren't, and can be changed, with "ashes

00:07:50.879 --> 00:07:52.069
of war".

00:07:52.069 --> 00:07:55.060
When you sit at a grace, select the Ash of
War option.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:08:01.319
Here you can see all your basic weapons, but
also bows, catalysts, talismans and shields.

00:08:01.319 --> 00:08:04.039
Remember to give them ashes of war as well.

00:08:04.039 --> 00:08:19.169
Ashes of War come with a skill, but also a
couple of scaling options.

00:08:19.169 --> 00:08:22.160
Be sure to pick the scaling that best suits
your stats.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:29.069
Oh, and don't forget.

00:08:29.069 --> 00:08:37.750
Kick is now an L2 skill, and can be performed
when your bare fists are out.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:43.890
It functions similarly to Dark Souls, punishing
enemies severely if they have their shield

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.460
up.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:48.600
8 - Powerstancing

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:54.220
Seeing a return in Elden Ring is powerstancing
- allowing you to draw additional benefit

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:59.620
from dual wielding, as long as both weapons
you have equipped are of the same type.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:02.320
Here, for example, I have two greatswords.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:08.220
Even though one is the crucible greatsword
and one is a bastard sword, both are greatswords,

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.260
so both can be powerstanced.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:15.270
When I tap L1, I attack with both weapons,
dramatically increasing my damage and giving

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:25.720
me access to a powerful moveset.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.722
This L1 can also be used in running attacks..but
perhaps most importantly, you can now also

00:09:30.722 --> 00:09:33.950
do powerstanced L1 jumping attacks.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:41.160
These are particularly useful while powerstancing
because they're a high-mobility attack, and

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:48.720
mobility is EVERYTHING when you don't have
a shield equipped.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:53.940
This is also a great time to mention that
your jump also has iframes, allowing you to

00:09:53.940 --> 00:10:04.080
dodge through enemy attacks AND queue up an
attack at the same time.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:09.230
Of course, you don't need to powerstance to
do this - every weapon has access to R1 and

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.830
even heavy R2 jumping attacks, as well.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:12.830
9 - Mount

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:16.850
One of the best ways to utilise jumping attacks
is off the back of your mount.

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:21.100
Dismount with L3, and slam them with L1, R1,
or R2.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:26.850
The distance you cover with this is absurd,
and initiating a fight in this way gives you

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.660
an immediate advantage.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:34.840
You can also dismount with the same whistle
item you use to mount, but I'd recommend getting

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:41.120
into the habit of using L3 instead, since
you'll commonly quick swap off the whistle

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.100
in order to heal.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:48.221
Crimson flasks heal your character on horseback,
but they don't heal your mount, which CAN

00:10:48.221 --> 00:10:50.820
take damage as well.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:55.430
Torrent's health bar is pretty enormous, but
if a fight goes on long enough, it's possible

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:57.060
for him to die.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:01.310
If this happens, you'll have to sacrifice
a crimson flask to revive him.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:07.630
Instead, if you notice torrent taking a ton
of damage, heal him instead - rowa berries

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:12.500
found throughout the world can be used to
craft rowa raisins, which can be fed to Torrent

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:13.500
while mounted.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.920
Before Torrent takes enough damage to die,
it's far more likely that you'll be knocked

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.800
off your horse instead.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:23.900
This is done when your posture is broken,
and it puts you in a vulnerable state on the

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:27.240
ground for a really..really long time.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:32.880
This is devastating, so it's probably a good
idea to fight on-foot after you've fought

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:37.060
on your mount for a little while.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:41.770
While mounted, you can double jump to get
over more terrain, and sprint to move across

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:43.360
it quickly.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:48.490
Interestingly, you don't have to HOLD circle
to sprint..you just have to tap it.

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:55.081
Tapping it gives you a burst of speed in exchange
for stamina, so remember to spam it when you're

00:11:55.081 --> 00:11:58.410
desperately trying to outrun something, like
a dragon's flame.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:03.020
Of course, while out of combat, sprinting
doesn't consume stamina at all.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:09.170
While mounted, R1 and R2 give you light and
heavy attacks on the right side, and L1 and

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:12.330
L2 give light and heavy attacks on your left
side.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:18.660
If you hold your heavy attacks, you can charge
them for a while in order to properly time

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:20.270
their release.

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:26.010
Interestingly, most weapons seem to have active
hitboxes WHILE you're charging the attack.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:32.500
Some, like the lance seem to have a higher
hitbox, good for mounted enemies.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:38.260
Others, like the greatsword, are dragged along
the ground, excellent for dispatching grounded

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.270
enemies.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:43.860
The Twinblade on the other hand seemed to
have a very inconsistent hitbox while spinning,

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:47.430
so it's possible there are advantages and
disadvantages to each.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.700
There are a variety of ways to take out enemies
on horseback.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:55.760
You can target and kill their horse, then
fight the enemy alone....or you can target

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:59.850
them on horseback, and kill them to leave
their horse wandering.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:04.870
Some enemies can be instantly knocked off
with sleep arrows..though horses seem to be

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:11.880
immune..or even with certain spells that deal
a ton of posture damage.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:18.160
All of this is good, but the most stylish
way to take out a mounted enemy, is this:

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.530
A well-timed parry.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:20.910
10 - Day &amp; Night

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.550
This black horseman can only be fought at
night.

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:28.220
He patrols this bridge back and forth..and
it's in exactly the same manner as another

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:29.890
horseman does at day.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:35.540
I even camped out here for a full day to try
and see if this daytime knight transforms

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:40.850
into the night..knight..and..he does, but
there's no transformation.

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:44.500
So this brings me to the day and night system.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:49.030
In Elden Ring, a full day and night takes
exactly one hour to pass.

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:52.130
I know this, because I sat and timed the whole
thing.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:58.380
The sun rises and sets in real time, rain
starts, rain stops..and all of it is a fantastic

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:01.470
addition to the game that really makes the
world feel alive.

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:07.350
But the true test of this system is its gameplay
implications..and so far, there are a few.

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:13.680
We mentioned the black knight, but bats also
spawn in more locations at night.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:19.280
Overall, night seems like it contains more
difficult enemies..so if you prefer, you can

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:34.530
sit at a grace and pass time until morning.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:47.380
This same time dial can be found any time
on your map screen, where it's even more specific

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:51.200
about the time of day..telling you whether
it's morning, afternoon, evening, and so-on.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.410
I bet, and sincerely hope, that specific events
can only be found at these specific times

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.410
of day.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.410
One benefit to night is that it seems to buff
your stealth.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:57.950
The results of my test are on-screen: as you
can see here, this enemy spotted me here during

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:58.950
the day....and..here, at night.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:14:59.950
I got far closer without being detected.

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:00.950
So if you're sneaking into a camp, perhaps
to grab a valuable item like the map fragment

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.500
in this camp..that's another excellent reason
to set your time of day at the Grace checkpoint.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:09.520
..and if you get really close to enemies you
might be able to overhear..yup, I knew it.

